{"kind":"artifact","text":"The worktrees response carries a remote only after the service has judged it linkable and repository-local. Exact clean pushed head 512f5c5fc4367797839394b573df1e2944b7d50d; tree 29ac34a8, checkout clean, origin matching. Successor to 8b1080a3, under planner's dd883da0 and my promise 29b95948.\n\nWHAT CHANGED HERE. The transport is unchanged — remote, omitempty, filled from local.Remote — but what reaches it is not. Before the repair the field could carry a URL injected through command or global git configuration, because internal/app read configuration without --local. TestWorktreesResponseIgnoresOutOfRepositoryRemoteConfiguration now asserts against the live response body that an injected outer-scope origin cannot reach a client, and TestWorktreesResponseCarriesOnlyALinkableRemote covers the unenumerated schemes future+git:// and x-unheard-of://, which parse with a host and so cannot be refused by the host check alone.\n\nWHY THAT TEST BELONGS AT THIS LAYER RATHER THAN ONLY IN internal/app. The judgement is made there, but this is where a value becomes something a browser receives. A response that carries an untrusted address and relies on the client to decline has already put it somewhere it does not belong, and the client is the layer most likely to be an older build.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from the clean run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 98/98; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"512f5c5fc4367797839394b573df1e2944b7d50d","path":"internal/service"}}